    <string name="native_hint">Eye tab: pupil diameter is wire raw ÷ 10 in mm, with raw values also shown. Openness uses 0–1; direction components use −1…1 (head-relative right/up/back; forward is −Z). Flags follow the Avatar E encoder, including normal-mode per-eye gaze filtering. Independent gaze always filters per-eye validity; see its actual E packet in Sent packet details. No estimated pupil is substituted.</string>
    <string name="outputs_title">Sent packet details</string>
    <string name="outputs_hint">Source snapshots are listed first; unknown expression slots use NaN and unobserved native values are labeled. The packet sections retain the last successful UDP sends, not proof of PC receipt or current values. Check each sourceNs and epoch: historical packets can belong to older sessions. “not sent” means no successful send on that route this service run. Values retain source/encoded precision, with header, quality and clock fields. Samples are not written to logs.</string>
